      "writtenOn": "2025-01-06T08:51:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added more comments and moved the common operation of getting timestamp higher up. If this is still not clear let me know I will add more details.\n\nIf we have something like A-\u003eB-\u003eC and C turns out to be a long running method, then we will have A entry, B entry, C entry, C exit in the buffer. When B exits we will see C exit as a previous event so we know that there was a long running method somewhere so we just record B\u0027s exit as well. Similarly we will record for A exit as well. \n\nIf C wasn\u0027t a long running methd, then we would have A entry, B entry in the buffer. When we see B exit, the previous event will be B\u0027s entry. We then check if B was long running or not. If B wasn\u0027t long running either we erase B entry.",
      "parentUuid": "789575e8_7dd71f76",
